# Rates: two beakers, one variable, one clock.
#
# The disappearing cross. Thiosulfate and acid make sulfur, the sulfur
# clouds the liquid, and the time it takes to hide a mark under the beaker
# is the measurement. Nothing here is scripted: both beakers run the same
# rate law, and the only difference between them is temperature.
register lv2

add v1 water 100mL
add v1 Na2S2O3 0.79g
add v1 HCl 0.002mol

new
add v2 water 100mL
add v2 Na2S2O3 0.79g
add v2 HCl 0.002mol
heat v2 8kJ

# Time is shared. `wait` advances the whole bench, which is the only way a
# fair test means anything.
wait 20s
look v1
look v2

wait 40s
look v1
look v2
